The table structure information is ({database name: {schema name: [table name]}}): 
{'bigquery-public-data': {'fhir_synthea': ['patient', 'condition', 'medication_request']}}
Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and their possible usage  
------------------------------------------------  
patient.id   : join‐key that uniquely identifies each patient  
patient.deceased.dateTime   : NULL  ⇒  patient is still alive  
condition.subject.patientId   : join‐key to patient.id  
condition.code.text / condition.code.coding (UNNEST).display   : look‑up strings that contain “diabetes” or “hypertension”  
condition.clinicalStatus / verificationStatus   : optional filter for confirmed / active diagnoses  
medication_request.subject.patientId   : join‐key to patient.id  
medication_request.status   : we want only records whose status = 'active'  
medication_request.medication.codeableConcept.coding.code or .display (UNNEST)   : medication identifier; use DISTINCT to count per patient  

Typical conditions you may use  
• patient.deceased.dateTime IS NULL  
• LOWER(condition.code.text) LIKE '%diabetes%' OR …  
• medication_request.status = 'active'  
• HAVING COUNT(DISTINCT med_code) ≥ 7  

Ten exploratory BigQuery SQL queries  
------------------------------------  

```sql
-- 1. Inspect a few patients and their deceased flag
SELECT id, deceased.dateTime
FROM `bigquery-public-data.fhir_synthea.patient`
LIMIT 20;
